1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:26,000
SPEAKERA: Around two hundred and forty BC, a scholar in Egypt worked out the size of the whole Earth.

2
00:00:31,000 --> 00:00:56,000
SPEAKERB: Without ever going round it?

3
00:01:01,000 --> 00:01:26,000
SPEAKERA: He didn't need to. He used a shadow, a distance and one idea from geometry.

4
00:01:31,000 --> 00:01:56,000
SPEAKERB: And his answer was about 250,000 stadia.

5
00:02:01,000 --> 00:02:26,000
SPEAKERA: Which sounds precise. But even today, we can't say exactly how close he came.

6
00:02:31,000 --> 00:02:56,000
SPEAKERB: So this is the story of Eratosthenes, and of a number we still argue about.

7
00:03:01,000 --> 00:03:26,000
SPEAKERB: Eratosthenes was born around 276 BC in Cyrene, a Greek city in what's now Libya.

8
00:03:31,000 --> 00:03:56,000
SPEAKERA: He studied in Athens for years. Then the king of Egypt, Ptolemy the Third, called him to Alexandria.

9
00:04:01,000 --> 00:04:26,000
SPEAKERB: To run the Library of Alexandria, one of the largest libraries of the ancient world.

10
00:04:31,000 --> 00:04:56,000
SPEAKERA: Quite a job offer.

11
00:05:01,000 --> 00:05:26,000
SPEAKERA: And the post came with another duty: tutor to the future king.

12
00:05:31,000 --> 00:05:56,000
SPEAKERB: He wrote about mathematics, geography, poetry, history and the stars.

13
00:06:01,000 --> 00:06:26,000
SPEAKERA: His admirers called him Pentathlos, like an athlete who competes in five events.

14
00:06:31,000 --> 00:06:56,000
SPEAKERB: And his critics called him Beta: second best at everything.

15
00:07:01,000 --> 00:07:26,000
SPEAKERA: Second best at everything is still quite something.

16
00:07:31,000 --> 00:07:56,000
SPEAKERB: One thing he didn't have to prove was that the Earth is round.

17
00:08:01,000 --> 00:08:26,000
SPEAKERA: They already knew that?

18
00:08:31,000 --> 00:08:56,000
SPEAKERB: For a century or so. Aristotle had pointed to the Earth's round shadow on the Moon during an eclipse.

19
00:09:01,000 --> 00:09:26,000
SPEAKERA: And he noted that some stars seen in Egypt can't be seen from further north.

20
00:09:31,000 --> 00:09:56,000
SPEAKERB: Which only works if the ground curves between the two places.
